                        "review": "Edit 3.Feb.2017: Uhm, so Dharker studio removed his dev response from this review. Not to worry I archived that long ago :)\n\nDev Response from Dharker Studio about this review:\n\nhttp://i.imgur.com/LK2uiI4.png\n\nIt's sad seeing this game getting positive reviews when most of them are trying to be funny. \n\nReview starts here!!!\n\nI was a backer during on kickstarter for this project, and let me start off by saying that this game is not worth the price.\n\nIf you are looking for something ecchi or even a good story look for other visual novels.\n\nPros:\n *Made by a western team\n *The game art brings up the game standard\n\nCons:\n *Mouth animations are way off, if done right it would be a perfect feature but this just ruins the voice acting\n\t*Example, when the text says Hmmm? the mouth will move as if the person were talking\n *The price is to high for the amount of gameplay.. Heh I even got this for £20 when i backed it, look at the price now\n *Rushed story\n *Total of 9 endings, 2 of which are at the start so you can barely call them a proper ending.\n     *Most of the choices you make won't have a big effect on anything. Only 1 choice will really make an impact on certain endings\n *The volume of the voice acting is not leveled, it'll go from low to high in the most weird places\n *Music is tiring and doesn't add anything, would suggest turning it off\n *\"A new day dawns.\" That is not a clock.\n *Mediocre voiceacting\n\nI was banned from the steam community of Divine slice of Life for posting about review manipulation.. So clearly trying to silence me I guess.. Don't filter opinions for the public to see.. \nThe respond can be found here: http://i.imgur.com/oLO2ih1.png\nPM if you are interested in the entire post I made about the review manipulation. :> \nGiving someone the game key and writing the review for them is still manipulation, even if you want to go with the \"friends\" part.\nTrying to avoid a launch like Beach Bounce.. Make a better game then. And don't make the focus \"making money\" over making a game for people to enjoy.",
